body:
## Bevy version

0.6.0

## What you did

Apply the following patch to bevy source tree (git apply patch.txt)
```rust
diff --git a/examples/ui/button.rs b/examples/ui/button.rs
index 48e67b55..a526f854 100644
--- a/examples/ui/button.rs
+++ b/examples/ui/button.rs
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@ fn main() {
         .add_plugins(DefaultPlugins)
         .add_startup_system(setup)
         .add_system(button_system)
+        .add_system(ui_size)
         .run();
 }
 
@@ -73,3 +74,9 @@ fn setup(mut commands: Commands, asset_server: Res<AssetServer>) {
             });
         });
 }
+
+pub fn ui_size(q: Query<&Node, Changed<Node>>) {
+    for node in q.iter() {
+        bevy::log::warn!("Node size change: {:?}", node);
+    }
+}
```

And run `cargo run --example button`

## What you expected to happen

Should print a line only when the UI size actually changes (e.g. when resizing a window).

## What actually happened

This will print UI Node change on each frame:
```
2022-01-27T20:30:42.762507Z  WARN button: Node size change: Node { size: Vec2(150.0, 65.0) }
2022-01-27T20:30:42.778312Z  WARN button: Node size change: Node { size: Vec2(104.0, 40.0) }
2022-01-27T20:30:42.778373Z  WARN button: Node size change: Node { size: Vec2(150.0, 65.0) }
2022-01-27T20:30:42.796493Z  WARN button: Node size change: Node { size: Vec2(104.0, 40.0) }
```
(note the two separate entities with different sizes)

